nventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HONDA MASAKUNI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUO KENRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO KOUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HONDA, MASAKUNI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUO, KENRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, KOUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A moving sidewalk having, ahead and behind a main circulating belt (27), independent getting-on and getting-off belts (21, 51) and one or plurality of accelerating/decelerating belts (22 to 25, 52, 53), the traveling speeds of the getting-on/getting-off belts and the accelerating/decelerating belts being gradually slower for belts gradually closer to the entrance or exit sides and gradually faster for belts gradually closer to the main circulating belt, of which traveling speed is set to be the fastest, wherein speeds of adjacent belts are set so that the difference between squares of the speeds of these belts does not exceed a specified value.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un trottoir roulant, comprenant en amont et en aval une bande principale (27) de circulation, des bandes d'accès et de descente (21, 51), et une ou plusieurs bandes d'accélération/décélération (22 à 25, 52, 53), la vitesse de déplacement des bandes d'accès/descente et des bandes d'accélération/décélération étant graduellement réduite pour les bandes se trouvant les plus proches des côtés entrée ou sortie, et graduellement augmentée pour les bandes se trouvant les plus proches de la bande principale de circulation dont la vitesse de déplacement est réglée pour être la plus rapide, les vitesses des bandes adjacentes étant réglées de sorte que la différence entre les carrés des vitesses de ces bandes ne dépassent pas une valeur spécifiée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>